 with water leaking into the goggles, swam away from the rest to record his sixth world record at the distance. Behind him " [:a {:href "/athletes/103162"} "László Cseh, Jr."] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/103189"} "Takeshi Matsuda"] " became the second and third swimmers to break 1:53 for the distance. The victory brought Phelps’ gold medal tally up into double figures to either equal " [:a {:href "/athletes/78385"} "Ray Ewry"] "’s record of 10 Olympic victories or break the record of nine held by four other Olympians. This depends on your view of the official status of the 1906 Olympic Games."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/93860"} "Michael Phelps"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1:53.70 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "1:53.70 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "1:52.03 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/103162"} "László Cseh, Jr."]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "1:54.48 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "1:54.35 (3 h1)"] [:td {} "1:52.70 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/103189"} "Takeshi Matsuda"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} "1:55.06 (3 h6)"] [:td {} "1:54.02 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "1:52.97 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:clas